{
  "metadata": {
    "name": "Czech phoneme inventory",
    "notes": "Czech phoneme inventory on the 27 features of romanian_features.json, in the same order, labelled as cs-IPA (en.wiktionary {{cs-IPA}}, the transcription convention of the Czech data) writes the segments. Segments shared with Romanian (a o u p b t d k ɡ t͡s t͡ʃ d͡ʒ f v s z ʃ ʒ m n l r j) copy its values exactly. Vowels: short ɪ ɛ (cs-IPA writes short i/y as ɪ and e/ě as ɛ) have the bundles of Romanian i e; the long vowels iː ɛː aː oː uː add Long + (length is contrastive: Stress stays -, Tense stays 0 on every vowel as in Romanian). r̩ l̩ are r l with Syllabic + (vlk, krk, bratr). u̯ is the offglide of the diphthongs ou̯ au̯ ɛu̯ and has the bundle of Romanian w. New consonants: c ɟ ɲ (ť ď ň) are t d n with Anterior - and Distributed +, a plain coronal place with DORSAL - and the tongue-body features 0 (as Italian ɲ), so t > ť d > ď n > ň is a pure place fill; x is k with Continuant + and DelRel 0; ɦ is x with Voice +: it is phonologically the voicing partner of x (sníh [sɲiːx], cs-IPA dechberoucí [dɛɦbɛrou̯t͡siː]) and alternates with z ʒ like ɡ, so it is coded dorsal, not as a laryngeal (its glottal articulation is phonetic). r̝ (ř) is r with Sonorant -, Approximant - (an obstruent: it devoices and joins voicing assimilation, JIPA 2012) and the place of c ɟ ɲ (Anterior -, Distributed +), so r > ř is the same place fill as t > ť and n > ň; Trill + and Lateral - keep it apart from ʒ, and Strident stays 0 as on r. Conventions as in Romanian: every segment is + or - for LABIAL CORONAL DORSAL; Anterior and Distributed are 0 unless CORONAL +; velars are DORSAL + with the tongue-body features 0; DelRel is - on oral stops (c ɟ included), + on affricates, 0 elsewhere. Allophones are not listed: ŋ (n before velars), ɱ, the voiceless r̝̊ (ř after a voiceless obstruent or finally), ɣ (= ɦ under this coding), d͡z and the glottal stop; the Czech tokenizer folds r̝̊ ŋ ɱ ɣ onto r̝ n m ɦ and skips ʔ. g and h occur only in loans and fold onto ɡ ɦ. The analysis (phonology/analyses/czech_palatalization.py) declares its patches and underspecified segments on top of this file; the choices are argued in docs/czech/phonology.md."
  },
